#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.14/site-packages/pygmt/src/grdproject.py:docstring
#: of pygmt.src.grdproject.grdproject:3
msgid ""
"This method will project a geographical gridded data set onto a rectangular "
"grid. If ``inverse`` is ``True``, it will project a rectangular coordinate "
"system to a geographic system. To obtain the value at each new node, its "
"location is inversely projected back onto the input grid after which a value "
"is interpolated between the surrounding input grid values. By default bi-"
"cubic interpolation is used. Aliasing is avoided by also forward projecting "
"the input grid nodes. If two or more nodes are projected onto the same new "
"node, their average will dominate in the calculation of the new node value. "
"Interpolation and aliasing is controlled with the ``interpolation`` "
"parameter. The new node spacing may be determined in one of several ways by "
"specifying the grid spacing, number of nodes, or resolution. Nodes not "
"constrained by input data are set to NaN. The ``region`` parameter can be "
"used to select a plot region larger or smaller than that implied by the "
"extent of the grid file."
msgstr ""

